# Patches applied to the engine source, in order.
#
# One file per concern, named NNN-subsystem-what.patch. Keep them small and
# single-purpose: a 2000-line patch touching six subsystems cannot be rebased
# when upstream moves, and rebasing is the main recurring maintenance cost.
#
# Prefer the least invasive layer that works:
#   1. A GN arg or runtime flag              (no patch at all - always try first)
#   2. A bundled component/extension          (no engine change)
#   3. A patch                                (last resort - you own it forever)
#
001-gl-allow-angle-opengl-on-mac.patch
# Grol's agent is a component extension shipped in the app bundle: not listed
# in chrome://extensions, cannot be disabled or removed.
002-extensions-bundle-grol-agent.patch
# New tabs and the startup tab open the agent page instead of Google's NTP.
003-ntp-open-grol-page.patch
# Tabs run down the side by default (tab groups = sections with sub-tabs);
# the tab strip menu switches back to horizontal.
004-tabs-vertical-by-default.patch
# Browser frame / tab strip tinted Grol violet (neutral) by default.
005-theme-grol-violet-default.patch
# Unnamed tab groups show "Untitled group" instead of an empty bar.
006-tabs-label-unnamed-groups.patch
# No "Customize" footer under the Grol home page.
007-ntp-no-footer.patch
# The app selects its GL backend itself (no Metal in this build), so it
# renders correctly when opened from Finder/Dock, not only from run.sh.
008-mac-default-gpu-flags.patch
# Code-sign clone off until Grol ships Developer ID signed releases.
009-mac-no-code-sign-clone.patch
# No "Google API keys are missing" bar (Grol uses the user's Gemini key).
010-startup-no-api-keys-infobar.patch
# Skip the upstream welcome screen; Grol onboards the user itself.
011-startup-skip-welcome.patch
# (UI text branding is applied by scripts/brand-strings.py, not a patch.)
